pgmetrics: read log timestamps in the server's log_timezone

Log timestamps (%m, %t and csvlog) end in a zone abbreviation of log_timezone.
time.Parse resolves an abbreviation only within the process's local zone and
reads any other as offset 0, so with log_timezone different from the time zone
of the pgmetrics host (an agent container in UTC, a server in Europe/Moscow)
times were shifted by the zone offset: east of UTC entries landed in the
future and were collected again by the next run, west of UTC they fell out of
the --log-span window and nothing was collected. Timestamps are now parsed in
the location named by log_timezone; an abbreviation that location does not
know is read as wall time there. Build with -tags timetzdata where the host has
no time zone database.

